---
number: 556
title: As We See the Day Approaching
author: Anonymous
composer: John Zundel
sp_category: "37"
topic: The Second Coming of Jesus
---

[verse 1]
As we see the day approaching
And Thy coming drawing near.
We rejoice in Thee with trembling,
While we serve Thee, Lord, with fear.
Soon that day, foretold, expected,
And for which we’ve hoped so long,
Will, in rapture, burst upon us
With a resurrection song.

[verse 2]
We would so abide in Thee, Lord,
That when Thou shalt soon appear,
We, with boldness, may salute Thee,
Knowing nought of slavish fear:
For, with this bright hope upon Thee,
We our lives would purify,
Not to be ashamed before Thee
When we meet Thee in the sky.

[verse 3]
Some of us may sleep in Jesus
E’er that holy day shall be:
Whether sleeping, whether walking,
We shall rise and live with Thee.
So amid the present darkness
We will comfort each his heart;
We shall “all be changed,” be like Thee
And be with Thee where Thou art.
